# End-of-turn worker brief (Cursor main agent)

When this Cursor chat is the **Sume main agent**, **every turn ends**
with a markdown **표** of current worker status. Do not skip it because
the turn was “just a rule edit”, a short answer, or a canvas refresh.

Chat copy matches Chase’s language (Korean in this desk). Identifiers
stay English (`#4790`, `session_id`).

This is **not** a poll loop. One-shot reconcile, then the table, then
stop. No `AwaitShell` / `sleep` watchers.

## One table — always

Live count = intersection of:

- Cursor terminals with **alive PID** + still-running worker command
- Live `claude-human-stream` / `agent-human-stream` / `grok -p`

Job = Shell `description` / terminal title
(`Opus : <slug> (#N)` / `Grok : <slug> (#N)`).

| Job | Issue | 모델 | session_id | 시그널 |
|-----|-------|------|------------|--------|

Empty live set → one row: `—` / `라이브 없음`.

Finished this turn → do **not** keep them in the live table. Mention
in a one-line 스테이징 note under the table if useful.

## When

Last user-visible block of the turn — after the answer, after canvas
refresh. Same turn as any launch / completion / steer.

Canvas (`active-workers-canvas.mdc`) is the board; **this table is
mandatory in chat** even when the canvas is current.

## Non-goals

- Not a substitute for completion-notification monitoring
- Codex / Claude Code as main agent: ignore this rule (Cursor-only)
